@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Research
+
+## Request paths and current causes
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductApi.java` maps `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}` to `ProductCommonFacadeImpl.deleteProduct`, which calls `ProductService.delete`. Deletion removes the live `Product` and related catalog data; it does not preserve a product relationship in carts or orders.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v2/product/ProductApiV2.java` maps `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` to `ProductFacadeV2Impl.getProductByCode`. That facade already raises `ResourceNotFoundException` when the SKU lookup returns null, so deleted products should naturally remain 404.
+
+## Carts
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` reloads each persisted cart item by SKU in `getPopulatedItem`. A missing product sets `item.obsolete=true`; `getPopulatedShoppingCart` then sets the whole cart obsolete, and `getByCode`/`getById` deletes/returns null for an obsolete cart. This is why a cart containing a deleted product cannot be opened.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/cart/ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java` assumes every cart item has a live `Product` and passes `item.getProduct()` to `ReadableMinimalProductMapper`, so retaining an orphaned cart item would still fail conversion.
+- `ShoppingCartServiceImpl.getPopulatedItem` also recalculates price and subtotal from the live product. A deleted line must therefore be removed from the persisted cart before calculation/serialization; remaining lines can continue through the existing repricing path.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` creates cart items through `productService.getBySku`; missing products are rejected, with the persistable-cart entry path using `ResourceNotFoundException`. This is the correct 404 behavior for adding a deleted SKU and must remain true for single and multi-item mutations.
+- Checkout converts cart items to order products in `OrderProductPopulator`, then `OrderServiceImpl` decrements inventory. The latter currently calls `productService.getById(orderProduct.getId())`; `OrderProduct.id` is not `Product.id`, so this is an existing ID mismatch and must use the SKU/live product lookup, while deleted cart lines must never reach checkout.
+
+## Orders
+
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/order/orderproduct/OrderProduct.java` is already a snapshot: it persists SKU, product name, ordered quantity, one-time charge, attributes, prices, and downloads. It has no `Product` association.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java` and the deprecated `ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java` correctly populate the snapshot fields, but optionally look up the current product by SKU to attach a live product projection. That optional lookup must stay optional; deleted products should still serialize the snapshot fields.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/order/OrderFacadeImpl.java` converts order products through the mapper for confirmation/read responses, so mapper null-tolerance covers merchant and customer order reads and lists. Order totals are read from persisted `OrderTotal` rows and are not recalculated from the catalog product.
+- `OrderServiceImpl` persists order products independently, but its inventory update assumes a live product exists. Checkout requirements are satisfied by filtering deleted cart lines before order creation; the inventory lookup should nevertheless use SKU and tolerate a missing product rather than making order persistence depend on `OrderProduct.id`.
+
+## Other affected behavior
+
+- Product deletion itself should not be broadened to delete carts or orders. Existing product cleanup (images, reviews, relationships, catalog row) remains intact.
+- Empty carts must remain persisted and readable with an empty product collection, quantity 0, and calculated subtotal/total 0 so they can still be mutated and checked out.
+- The modern cart mapper and legacy cart populator both need to tolerate an empty line-item set; the modern API paths use `ReadableShoppingCartMapper`.
+
+## Intended change boundary
+
+1. During cart hydration, remove missing-SKU items (and their cart attributes) from the cart instead of marking the whole cart obsolete; persist the cleaned set and keep the cart.
+2. Make cart serialization skip any defensive orphan item and calculate from surviving items.
+3. Keep add/multi-add missing-product validation mapped to 404.
+4. Make order snapshot conversion independent of a live product and fix checkout inventory lookup to use SKU/missing-product tolerance.
+5. Add focused regression tests where the existing test structure permits, then run Maven verification.
